# The Markdown files of the tree, one glob a line. A `*` matches any run of
# characters within one segment of a path. The rule `markdown` of
# `tree-rules` refuses each tracked Markdown file that no glob matches. Its
# prose goes into rustdoc.
# - see: `crates/workflow-tree-rules`
#
# The list holds each README, the changelog, the census of the ledger, and
# the templates of an issue and of a pull request. GitHub reads a template as
# Markdown. A literate sketch of the corpus is a program in Markdown, and the
# list holds it too.
# - see: #2896, #3112, #4723
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
crates/README.md
crates/*/README.md
contrib/*/README.md
library/*/README.md
ledger/README.md
ledger/census.md
.config/issues/templates/*.md
corpus/sketch/*/*.gandr.md
.github/pull_request_template.md
